2026-11-06T03:19:00.7035350Z [34m---- let's talk about sudo -----------------------------------------------------
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7044619Z [0mThis script is going to call sudo a lot. Normally, it would show you
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7045193Z exactly what commands it is running and why. However, the script is
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7045744Z run in a headless fashion, like this:
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7046144Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7046362Z   $ curl -L https://nixos.org/nix/install | sh
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7046686Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7046954Z or maybe in a CI pipeline. Because of that, I'm going to skip the
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7047518Z verbose output in the interest of brevity.
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7047853Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7047996Z If you would like to
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7048366Z see the output, try like this:
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7048638Z 
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7048924Z   $ curl -L -o install-nix https://nixos.org/nix/install
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7049437Z   $ sh ./install-nix
2026-11-06T03:19:00.7049649Z 
